# What the container image build never reads (packaging/docker/Dockerfile builds from this
# checkout). Build OUTPUT is excluded rather than reused: the image compiles its own, against
# its own glibc, and a host `target/` is tens of gigabytes the daemon would copy first.
.git
target
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/.output
web/.tanstack
web/public/emoji
launcher/dist
launcher/server.embed
launcher/web.tar.gz
**/test-results
web/playwright-report
captures
.playwright-mcp
.worktrees
.atl

# An Intune ENROLLMENT BACKUP (`intune-container backup -o …`) holds the device's registration keys
# and its keyring, and packaging/docker/compose.yaml's import bind looks for one beside it — inside
# this build context, which the build stage copies whole (`COPY . .`). Sent to the daemon it would
# be kept in that stage's layer in the build cache after the file itself is gone, and leave the
# machine with any cache export. The same two patterns as .gitignore: it is never committed, and
# never built in.
packaging/docker/*.tar.gz
**/enrollment-backup*.tar.gz
